# Normalise text to LF in the repository. The artefact inventory hashes the blob Git stores, so a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true must not turn a tracked CSV into a different artefact than a
# Linux clone sees (A-38 is the post-mortem). Binary formats are declared so Git never touches them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.gif binary
# Checkpoints are stored in Git LFS from this commit on: the repository keeps a pointer whose oid is the
# file's SHA-256, so the artefact inventory still publishes the content hash (scripts/report_inventory.py).
# History before the switch keeps the full blobs; nothing was rewritten.
*.npz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
